# DOC format and Word COM (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/doc-format.md`, ADR-003)

## Invariants
- All Word COM work happens inside `word_com.word_session`: global non-reentrant `_WORD_COM_LOCK` (wait bounded by `WORD_COM_LOCK_TIMEOUT`), fresh `DispatchEx` WINWORD, `Quit` then `_kill_word_processes_started_after` fallback. Without psutil the fallback `taskkill`s **all** Word processes.
- `word_com.IS_AVAILABLE` is the single capability gate; never import `win32com` / `pywin32` outside `app/word_com.py`; never "fix" the import for Linux.
- Merge = `Selection.InsertFile` of a `sanitize_docx_for_insertion` copy (strips `<w:sectPr>`); the master document's layout always wins. Never docxcompose a DOC.
- Generation output is always DOCX; PDF is lazy via `GET /generate/pdf/<id>` (cached sibling; 503 when Word unavailable).
- Thumbnails: `DOC_THUMBNAIL_PATH/<asset_id>.png`, rendered lazily by `ensure_thumbnail` (first page → PDF → PyMuPDF PNG → post-processing). An IMG in the **same** `(question, asset_type, version)` slot eclipses the DOC (no thumbnail needed). Call `doc_thumbnails.on_*` lifecycle hooks **after `commit()`** on every IMG/DOC mutation.
- `_INFLIGHT` is cleared in `finally`; `_RETRY_COOLDOWN_S = 5`; `force_rerender` bypasses the cooldown. Poller: 60 × 3 s. Thumbnail endpoint keeps `Cache-Control: private, no-cache, must-revalidate`.
- Thumbnail settings (`DOC_THUMBNAIL_WIDTH`, `THUMBNAIL_*`) apply to new renders only → Health → Force Re-render All.
- `batch_image_gen` (DOC/MD → IMG) uses one `word_session` per run and whole-slot `replace_img_assets`.

## Gotchas
- `WORD_COM_TIMEOUT` exists in config/settings but is **not enforced**; there is no per-job watchdog today. Do not document one as if it existed; add it if a job hangs matter.
- Background renders run under `app.app_context()` with `app = current_app._get_current_object()` captured first.
- Word is single-instance: long queues show as lock waits, not parallelism.
